messages:
maria: Heads up — ran into a compatibility snag when trying to run the JS SDK inside a Cloudflare Worker. SDK's ESM build imports `node:crypto` and assumes `Buffer` exists. Worker throws at module init. Anyone seen this?
aj: yep, hit that last week. Cloudflare Workers don't have Node built-ins and no global Buffer. Which SDK entry did you import? the default `require('@redwood/inference')` or the ESM `import` path?
maria: using `import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference'` (ESM). It looks like our bundler picked up `node:crypto` via a tiny helper in the SDK that falls back to Node APIs for random bytes.
sven: common pattern. We have two axes here: runtime detection and packaging. For edge runtimes we should ship a build that avoids any node polyfills. Suggest we add a `worker`/`edge` entrypoint (e.g., `@redwood/inference/edge`) that only uses web crypto and doesn't reference `node:` imports.
claire: +1 on an explicit `edge` entrypoint. Also typings: TS complains because `Buffer` is used in types (e.g., `ArrayBuffer|Buffer`). That drags in `@types/node` sometimes. We should provide worker-friendly types or use conditional types like `Uint8Array | ArrayBuffer` in the public surface.
aj: for a quick workaround in app: shim Buffer and crypto before importing the SDK. Example we used in a worker: ```
// worker-shim.js
if (!globalThis.Buffer) {
  globalThis.Buffer = { from: (b) => new Uint8Array(b) }
}
globalThis.crypto = globalThis.crypto || self.crypto;
import { createClient } from '@redwood/inference'
```
That got us unblocked but feels hacky.
maria: thanks, that helped. But one more: the SDK's fetch wrapper expects Node Response/Request in error paths — threw when we tried streaming. Any thoughts for streaming compatibility?
sven: streaming differences are nasty. We added a small adapter in our app that normalizes to the WHATWG streams used in Workers. Could the SDK expose a tiny `adaptToFetchLike(runtime)` helper so apps can opt into worker mode? e.g., `import { createEdgeClient } from '@redwood/inference/edge'` that returns an instance with worker-friendly internals.
claire: also documenting recommended bundler configs would help. People using `esbuild`/`webpack`/`rollup` keep hitting different plumbings. For example, `esbuild` can shim node builtins with `--inject:node-shims.js` but we shouldn't promote that as the default. Better to provide: 1) edge ESM build (no node), 2) examples for Cloudflare/Wrangler, 3) a minimal worker template repo.
maria: agree — the onboarding friction is real. Could we add a check in SDK init that throws a helpful error when it detects a Node-only import in an edge runtime, with a pointer to docs? Right now it just fails during module evaluation.
devex-bot: Reminder: created ticket INF-412: "SDK: edge/worker entrypoint + docs + typing cleanup" and linked to repo issue.
aj: one more niche: Deno/Netlify Edge have global `crypto.subtle` but different `fetch` extensions (e.g., `Request` lacks some Node fields). Tests should run in a worker-like CI (miniflare) not only node. We had a CI job using `miniflare` to validate the worker bundle.
sven: good call. I'll upstream a tiny test harness that runs a smoke test in miniflare as part of the PR for the `edge` build. Also I'll add a small snippet for users: ```
// minimal worker example
import { createEdgeClient } from '@redwood/inference/edge'
addEventListener('fetch', event => {
  const client = createEdgeClient({ apiKey: SECRET })
  event.respondWith(handle(event.request))
})
async function handle(req){
  const r = await client.generate({ prompt: 'hi' })
  return new Response(await r.text())
}
```
claire: can we also simplify type exports so TS users don't accidentally pull `@types/node`? E.g., publish a `types/edge.d.ts` or conditionally export types via `types` field in package.json.
maria: thanks all — I'll add notes to the onboarding repo and link the worker template once sven has a PR. For now, workaround is the shim + miniflare CI.
aj: and I'll paste our small rollup config for anyone who needs it in the thread later.
sven: PR incoming this week, will ping everyone.
claire: thanks — can someone add a short blurb to the docs page under "Edge runtimes" with 1) recommended import (`@redwood/inference/edge`), 2) minimal worker snippet, 3) known limitations (no Node APIs, streaming caveats), and 4) CI suggestion (miniflare).
maria: filing a docs PR with checklist. closing the loop here, appreciate the quick help :thumbsup:
